      "text": "Minimum Perimeter of triangle XYZ \n\nTo find the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\), we first need to determine the lengths of its sides. The points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively in the right prism \\(ABCDEF\\) with a height of 16 and equilateral triangle bases of side length 12.\n\n1. **Identify the coordinates of the vertices:**\n   - Let \\(A = (0, 0)\\)\n   - \\(B = (12, 0)\\)\n   - \\(C = (6, -6)\\)\n   - \\(D = (6, -22)\\)\n   - \\(E = (0, -16)\\)\n   - \\(F = (12, -16)\\)\n\n2. **Find the coordinates of \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\):**\n   - \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\):\n     \\[\n     X = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3)\n     \\]\n   - \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\):\n     \\[\n     Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3)\n     \\]\n   - \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\):\n     \\[\n     Z = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-22-6}{2} \\right) = (6, -14)\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the distances \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(XZ\\):**\n   - Use the distance formula \\(d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\\).\n\n   For \\(XY\\):\n   \\[\n   XY = \\sqrt{(9 - 3)^2 + (-3 - (-3))^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n   \\]\n\n   For \\(YZ\\):\n   \\[\n   YZ = \\sqrt{(6 - 9)^2 + (-14 - (-3))^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + (-11)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\n   \\]\n\n   For \\(XZ\\):\n   \\[\n   XZ = \\sqrt{(6 - 3)^2 + (-14 - (-3))^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-11)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\):**\n   \\[\n   XY + YZ + XZ = 6 + \\sqrt{130} + \\sqrt{130} = 6 + 2\\sqrt{130}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + 2\\sqrt{130}}\n\\]",
